Lane A owns the movement engine. Do not apply this from lane D.

Oak starts on Champions Room warp (3, 7) and his exit step lands on warp
(3, 0). SourceActors rejects a script position on a warp, so those two cells
are not registered and NPCMotion:claimScript fails. The player follow is
pokered's simulated joypad (WalkToHallOfFame_RLEMovement): CollisionCheckOnLand
skips sprite and tile collision while wSimulatedJoypadStatesIndex is set, which
is how the player walks through the rival. EventState:startMove still rejects
an occupied cell.

EndgameStory.oakCells adds (3, 7) and (3, 0) once
SourceActors.championsOakMayCrossWarp exists. The champion plan sets
plan.simulated. Until both hunks land, a blocked step is skipped and the hall
warp still runs, so the ending does not get stuck. The lines and the walk
steps are already in the plan.

tools/tests/test_lane_d_endgame.py marks test_oak_can_cross_the_champion_warps
and test_simulated_follow_ignores_sprite_collision as expected failures.

